The patch chain no longer builds the app.

app/systole.html (with its carved pieces), src/ and assets/ are the source,
and scripts/assemble-app.js is the builder. scripts/build.js and the *-patch.js
steps stay in the repository as history, and as libraries where the assembler
imports from them (keys-patch, flags-patch, refs-patch, ref-images-patch,
heart-bake). Nothing is added to the chain.

Its presence is what scripts/release-check.js and npm run build read.
Delete it and the old path (and its byte-for-byte comparison) comes back,
for as long as app/ still equals the chain's output.

Retired 2026-10-04, at the owner's instruction. Before it: the assembled app
was byte-identical to the chain's build on the owner's machine at step 2, and
again on the real build after the stylesheet was carved (PR #139).
